00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,300
A man who learned the world's secrets,

258
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,640
probably alongside Rayleigh.

259
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:27,960
Yes, we know.

260
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:29,617
We learned all of it.

261
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:31,820
the entirety of the missing history.

262
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:37,017
So you're saying that Kaido was
using Doflamingo and Caesar to

263
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:40,417
try and learn these secrets of
the world or whatever from you?

264
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:42,740
since you guys were Odin's servants?

265
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:45,000
Yes, that's correct, Sorzoro.

266
00:17:46,820 --> 00:17:49,160
We know nothing on this subject matter.

267
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:54,153
Lord Odin made certain not to
burden us with any secrets.

268
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:57,152
Therefore, we possess no knowledge of it.

269
00:17:57,820 --> 00:18:01,996
Admittedly, if we were familiar with
it, we would not dare tell a soul.

270
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:06,300
Whether we know it or not,
we'll always be pursued.

271
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:12,040
That having been said, it leaves us with
just one choice, and that is to fight.

272
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:20,240
His final message before his
departure were these simple words.

273
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:21,520
Do it for me.

274
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:23,420
Open Wano's borders.

275
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:29,745
But why would he ask for that?

276
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:32,869
The land of Wano was
sealed from the world.

277
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:37,040
How shameful that our duty
was to protect Lord Odin.

278
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:39,940
And yet, in the end,
it was he who saved us.

279
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:43,400
Now we must go on with
this terrible disgrace.

280
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:46,080
We have shamed ourselves.

281
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:54,897
Our only solution is to ensure that
our master's dying wish is carried out.

282
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:58,317
We must kill the current
Shogun of Wano and

283
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:00,988
open the closed borders
of our dear country.

284
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:03,717
Achieving said feat is our deepest desire.

285
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:05,617
Yet we're in a quandary.

286
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:09,017
Due to the combined strength
of the Shogun and Kaido.

287
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:11,160
Wano's stuck in a Loguetown.

288
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:16,117
Back at home, the seeds of
rebellion are slowly being sown.

289
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:17,957
Yet we fall short.

290
00:19:18,040 --> 00:19:20,217
Our numbers are lacking as of yet.

291
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:23,660
And our victory is a distant hope.

292
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:26,980
I see quite the dilemma.

293
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:31,177
Still we all must win.

294
00:19:31,260 --> 00:19:36,177
Which is why in order to search
for allies that might assist us.

295
00:19:36,260 --> 00:19:38,537
We turned our attention to the sea.

296
00:19:38,620 --> 00:19:42,477
Our initial destination was to be Zo.

297
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:46,137
Yes, he speaks of our special bond.

298
00:19:46,220 --> 00:19:49,897
The Kozuki clan and the Mink
tribe have been aligned for ages.

299
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:52,197
And swore a pact to join our fates as one.

300
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:57,300
Above all else, me and the mutt here
were Lord Odin's direct vassals.

301
00:19:57,820 --> 00:19:59,620
Ever since Raizo showed up,

302
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:03,707
every one of our soldiers were
prepared for an inevitable war.

303
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:07,520
However, we underestimated the enemy.

304
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:13,800
It only took one of Kaido's troops
to leave us in this main state.

305
00:20:14,240 --> 00:20:16,064
Jack alone was too much for us.

306
00:20:18,320 --> 00:20:20,380
An embarrassing reality.

307
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:24,320
Boy, you're a disgrace, I know.

308
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:27,160
Hey, they pulled a dirty trick on you.

309
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:28,837
There's no need to beat yourself up.

310
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:29,750
Yeah,

311
00:20:29,833 --> 00:20:34,107
how could you have possibly known they
were going to use that awful poison gas?

312
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:36,880
Alas, sportsmanship
does not apply to wars.

313
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:42,040
No matter how vicious their game
plan, this is still our home country.

314
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:44,140
There are no excuses.

315
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:48,340
We shall not make the
same mistake next time.

316
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,440
From now on, we'll be prepared.

317
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:53,300
They shall soon realize.

318
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:58,780
They've yet to see our full potential as
we still have one final ace up our sleeve.

319
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:02,580
We have a request of you, Sir Luffy.

320
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:06,300
And you, Sir Law.

321
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:12,420
It pains me greatly to ask a favor
after you have saved our lives.

322
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:16,140
But your strength has astounded
me time and time again.

323
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:20,120
Undesperate, Sir Luffy, we need you.

324
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:22,820
As well as your crew, I beg you,

325
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:28,800
help us slay the Shogun of Wano and
strike down Kaido of the Four Emperors.

326
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:36,217
Whoa! Alright!

327
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:38,440
I'm all about this kind of alliance.

328
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:40,600
The Samurai and the Meek Tribe?

329
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:42,937
Now that's a lot of power at our disposal.

330
00:21:43,020 --> 00:21:46,117
I mean, we were gonna kick Kaido's
ass sooner or later, right?

331
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:48,117
Yeah, we gotta get in on this.

332
00:21:48,200 --> 00:21:50,100
They have a ninja! Yeah!

333
00:21:56,340 --> 00:21:57,260
I refuse.

334
00:21:59,780 --> 00:22:01,040
Come on, man!

335
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:03,377
But they are friends, aren't they?

336
00:22:03,460 --> 00:22:06,177
Do you need me to walk you
through why this is a good idea?

337
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,637
You can't pass this off!

338
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:09,320
Let's not rush into a no!

339
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:10,840
This is about unity!

340
00:22:13,060 --> 00:22:17,531
I'm gonna talk some sense into my buddy,
so could you give me a few minutes?

341
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,030
Stop it!

342
00:22:19,340 --> 00:22:21,260
Luffy, you should accept.

343
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:23,949
Or else we'll lose all
our respect for you.

344
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:25,330
Hold up.

345
00:22:27,460 --> 00:22:30,620
I think that Luffy
actually has a point here.

346
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:32,490
Mommy?

347
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:37,780
After all, we should negotiate.

348
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:40,160
Hurry, don't you dare!

349
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:48,240
What are you?

350
00:22:48,360 --> 00:22:50,000
A figurehead? Huh, Momo?

351
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,220
Knock it off!

352
00:22:52,460 --> 00:22:54,000
You're in charge, right?

353
00:22:54,620 --> 00:22:56,677
Aren't you the leader of these guys?

354
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:58,180
Say something already!

355
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:03,040
You just gonna cry?

356
00:23:14,740 --> 00:23:16,180
You're making him cry!

357
00:23:17,100 --> 00:23:19,440
Stop yelling at him, you big bully!

358
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:20,801
Now, now, Luffy.

359
00:23:20,920 --> 00:23:22,737
You're expecting far too much of him.

360
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:24,537
Heirs don't typically take
over the responsibilities

361
00:23:24,620 --> 00:23:26,777
of leadership until they come of age.

362
00:23:26,860 --> 00:23:29,566
Perhaps it's best if we
let the adults confer.

363
00:23:32,720 --> 00:23:33,760
Oh, Momonosuke?

364
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:37,577
That's right, sweet little Momo.

365
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:38,490
Come here.

366
00:23:38,580 --> 00:23:39,417
I'm sorry.

367
00:23:39,500 --> 00:23:42,500
Our idiot captain likes to
run his mouth sometimes.

368
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:59,040
Gaze out upon it, Momonosuke.

369
00:23:59,360 --> 00:24:02,740
This is the world, wider
than your imagination.

370
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:16,640
Father, I...

371
00:24:17,260 --> 00:24:18,980
We're surrounded, I fear!

372
00:24:21,040 --> 00:24:22,600
Father, help!

373
00:24:23,620 --> 00:24:25,480
Ready the flaming arrows!

374
00:24:27,820 --> 00:24:29,440
You must flee!

375
00:24:29,800 --> 00:24:31,212
Follow the escape route!

376
00:24:31,440 --> 00:24:33,180
Everyone, vacate!

377
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:38,860
Your father truly is?

378
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:42,220
A fool of a lord.

379
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:52,380
I want to vanquish Everikido!

380
00:24:54,780 --> 00:24:57,840
He was an enemy to both of my parents!

381
00:24:58,100 --> 00:25:01,460
And also responsible for
their untimely deaths!

382
00:25:02,620 --> 00:25:07,617
I want nothing more than to
grow up and become strong so

383
00:25:07,700 --> 00:25:11,288
that I may one day smite him
and avenge my mother and father!

384
00:25:11,900 --> 00:25:15,440
I wish to protect my
loyal servants as well!

385
00:25:17,220 --> 00:25:18,500
Lord Momonosuke!

386
00:25:19,980 --> 00:25:23,440
This little guy's grit,
he's moved me to tears.

387
00:25:24,020 --> 00:25:26,300
You Karoo are soft in your old age.

388
00:25:26,440 --> 00:25:27,440
Shut your muzzle!

389
00:25:28,140 --> 00:25:29,580
However, I'm powerless.

390
00:25:29,900 --> 00:25:31,900
I'm too small to assist in battle.

391
00:25:32,860 --> 00:25:36,900
That's why I must ask, will
you please help me fight?

392
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:43,360
Please loopy, I beg of you!

393
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:49,940
That's more like it.

394
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:58,020
Hey, Momo.

395
00:26:00,840 --> 00:26:02,157
Let's team up.

396
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:04,697
Just leave Kaido to me.

397
00:26:04,780 --> 00:26:06,140
And it's an alliance.

398
00:26:15,980 --> 00:26:18,877
Thank you from the bottom of my heart.

399
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:21,160
I am unworthy of such kindness.

400
00:26:21,620 --> 00:26:23,060
No, that's all wrong.

401
00:26:23,260 --> 00:26:25,740
Grab it tight like this. Go bam.

402
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:27,900
I cannot thank you enough.

403
00:26:28,340 --> 00:26:29,960
Come on, with more oomph.

404
00:26:31,140 --> 00:26:33,040
I am grabbing your hand.

405
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:34,140
No, this way.

406
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:37,800
I now see the point he was making.

407
00:26:38,360 --> 00:26:39,620
Go-roo-nya-nya-nya!

408
00:26:40,120 --> 00:26:41,940
An alliance is born.

409
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:44,238
Let's break out the booze and party.

410
00:26:45,620 --> 00:26:47,100
Hey, Straw Hat. Hmm?

411
00:26:47,960 --> 00:26:50,136
You should have run this by me first.

412
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:51,477
It's cool, right?

413
00:26:51,560 --> 00:26:54,320
It is, but still, how alleviating.

414
00:26:56,560 --> 00:26:59,780
Perhaps we should reflect
upon our attitudes. Huh?

415
00:27:00,880 --> 00:27:05,360
We were guilty of infantilizing him,
but he is the head of the Kozuki clan,

416
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:06,390
is he not?

417
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:10,257
Our drive to protect him had us
overlooking something so vital.

418
00:27:10,340 --> 00:27:13,417
True, Sir Luffy butted heads with a child.

419
00:27:13,500 --> 00:27:18,240
But remarkably, he also gave
him the courage to be a man.

420
00:27:19,100 --> 00:27:21,240
He is truly amazing.

421
00:27:22,900 --> 00:27:23,957
True indeed.

422
00:27:24,040 --> 00:27:27,860
I now understand your
respect for this pirate. Hmm.

423
00:27:36,100 --> 00:27:36,930
Okay.

424
00:27:37,013 --> 00:27:39,057
Let's gather around.

425
00:27:39,140 --> 00:27:40,800
Come on, everyone!

426
00:27:44,220 --> 00:27:46,080
Are we all ready?

427
00:27:51,040 --> 00:27:54,440
We're gonna kick Emperor
Kaido's ass together!

428
00:27:58,740 --> 00:28:03,800
It's Zero, the Ninja Pirate
Mink Samurai Alliance!

429
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:12,780
That's a mouthful.

430
00:28:13,240 --> 00:28:15,340
Do we need the ninja part?

431
00:28:15,540 --> 00:28:16,640
Of course we do!

432
00:28:17,120 --> 00:28:18,780
Okay, jeez.

433
00:28:35,920 --> 00:28:37,700
The target's Kaido!

434
00:28:37,960 --> 00:28:39,080
Let's do this!

435
00:28:39,680 --> 00:28:45,920
Dogstorm, Catviper, Momo, Kin'emon,
Kanjuro, Ninja Guy, and Traffy!

436
00:28:46,500 --> 00:28:50,257
I don't know anything about Kaido, but
with an alliance like this, he's toast.

437
00:28:50,340 --> 00:28:51,580
This is gonna be fun!

438
00:28:51,920 --> 00:28:55,780
By the way, don't you ever
bow your heads to me again.

439
00:28:56,160 --> 00:28:57,400
And don't kneel.

440
00:28:58,180 --> 00:29:00,337
Us being allies means...

441
00:29:00,420 --> 00:29:02,600
we're best friends, too!

442
00:29:02,820 --> 00:29:03,660
We are not!

443
00:29:03,920 --> 00:29:07,480
But if we're working together,
there is one condition. Hmm.

444
00:29:08,280 --> 00:29:09,680
Hmm? Hang on.

445
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:12,537
Perhaps that should have been
mentioned to us beforehand.

446
00:29:12,620 --> 00:29:13,855
What's the condition?

447
00:29:14,500 --> 00:29:17,676
Before we go anywhere, my
crew's down a man right now.

448
00:29:18,580 --> 00:29:19,410
Gotcha.

449
00:29:19,540 --> 00:29:20,940
This is about Sanji.

450
00:29:21,280 --> 00:29:22,140
What happened?

451
00:29:22,500 --> 00:29:24,960
I'm afraid that is a long story.

452
00:29:34,580 --> 00:29:35,410
Yugara?

453
00:29:35,493 --> 00:29:36,780
Mean the Big Mom?

454
00:29:36,980 --> 00:29:38,333
Why didn't you tell me?

455
00:29:38,580 --> 00:29:41,360
It all went down while
Yugara were napping.

456
00:29:42,100 --> 00:29:44,617
I'm gonna run off and
rescue him real quick.

457
00:29:44,700 --> 00:29:47,140
So hold off on fighting until I get back.

458
00:29:47,340 --> 00:29:49,340
Huh, that's your only condition.

459
00:29:49,660 --> 00:29:52,277
Well, if that's all, then
we shall gladly stand by.

460
00:29:52,360 --> 00:29:53,190
Thank you.

461
00:29:53,273 --> 00:29:55,593
And he's as strong as a thousand people.

462
00:29:56,100 --> 00:29:59,120
Trust me when I say this'll be worth it.

463
00:29:59,300 --> 00:30:01,240
Then I'm worth 2,000 people.

464
00:30:01,340 --> 00:30:02,640
Of course you are.

465
00:30:02,820 --> 00:30:03,720
I see, then.

466
00:30:03,900 --> 00:30:05,320
He'd be quite the asset.

467
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:07,960
However, take precaution.

468
00:30:08,140 --> 00:30:09,157
This is Big Mom.

469
00:30:09,240 --> 00:30:14,120
I'm not planning on fighting her,
and besides, I'll take Lion Viper.

470
00:30:14,300 --> 00:30:15,160
Wait, what?

471
00:30:15,440 --> 00:30:16,600
Who is that?

472
00:30:16,860 --> 00:30:18,360
Nyah-ha-ha-ha!

473
00:30:18,680 --> 00:30:19,920
Lion Viper?

474
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:21,540
Nyah-ha-ha!

475
00:30:27,920 --> 00:30:31,740
The miracles never cease
today, do they? No joke.

476
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:33,431
We couldn't predict this.

477
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:38,737
Those two had a rivalry so
strong they found it easier

478
00:30:38,820 --> 00:30:41,177
to split the day in half
rather than see each other,

479
00:30:41,260 --> 00:30:43,737
but they have finally settled
their differences—hard

480
00:30:43,820 --> 00:30:47,757
to believe—the moment has finally come,

481
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:50,077
and we're here to witness it.

482
00:30:50,160 --> 00:30:56,177
Supposedly, master Cat Viper and Duke
Dogstorm are once an inseparable pair;

483
00:30:56,260 --> 00:31:00,957
however, one day they came back
from a long voyage, barely alive.

484
00:31:01,040 --> 00:31:01,940
barely alive

485
00:31:02,620 --> 00:31:05,855
And it was like they had been
fighting all their lives.

486
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:10,437
Any time they even shared a glance,
it would cause an altercation.

487
00:31:10,520 --> 00:31:12,657
What could have happened between them?

488
00:31:12,740 --> 00:31:15,197
All that happened before
I was born, right?

489
00:31:15,280 --> 00:31:16,340
That'd be correct.

490
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:20,337
Pager and I were only little children when
those two returned from their journey.

491
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:22,277
Our two kings are friends again.

492
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:23,960
Let's throw a big feast!

493
00:31:25,300 --> 00:31:28,700
Now we can wake up or go to
sleep whenever we please!

494
00:31:49,700 --> 00:31:52,580
We have confirmation on
the target, Master Jack!

495
00:31:52,960 --> 00:31:54,800
You think I can't see it?

496
00:31:54,980 --> 00:31:55,840
It's huge!

497
00:31:56,720 --> 00:31:57,550
Damn it.

498
00:31:57,800 --> 00:31:59,859
I think I'd have to come back here.

499
00:32:02,120 --> 00:32:03,120
Sheep's head,

500
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:10,240
I didn't expect you to return to me and
report that Rhizo was not on the island.

501
00:32:10,740 --> 00:32:14,480
The Ming tribe is quite hardy. Tell me,

502
00:32:14,740 --> 00:32:17,597
what would happen if
those who escaped the gas

503
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:20,360
were able to nurse the
others back to health?

504
00:32:21,160 --> 00:32:23,600
That idiot better keep his mouth shut.

505
00:32:23,980 --> 00:32:28,157
If Master Jack finds out that they
survived and we got our asses handed to us,

506
00:32:28,240 --> 00:32:29,358
then we're screwed.

507
00:32:29,680 --> 00:32:34,137
When someone's on the brink of death,
you have to see it all the way through.

508
00:32:34,220 --> 00:32:36,200
Mercy only breeds vengeance.

509
00:32:38,100 --> 00:32:39,977
There's no need to worry, Master.

510
00:32:40,060 --> 00:32:42,707
If they're already
weakened, this'll be easy.

511
00:32:42,840 --> 00:32:45,117
We'll put the stragglers
out of their misery.

512
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:46,840
That won't be necessary.

513
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:53,740
We'll kill the elephant.

514
00:33:00,760 --> 00:33:03,560
Thank you.
